"color":"b","headline":"45…Re8! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["The rook takes the open e-file, aiming at the rook on e1 behind the bishop on e6.","Moves the attacked rook to safety.","The next best move, 45…Rf8, would drop Black's winning chances from 47% to 12% (+5.36).","45…Re8 gets the rook out of the way of Qxd8+ and takes the open e-file, aiming at the rook on e1 behind the bishop on e6.","White was threatening Qxd8+, winning a rook and a pawn. The rook steps away.","Shores up the bishop on e6, which was under as much attack as it had defence (2 against 1)."]},{"ply":92,"name":"46…Qa5","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"46…Qa5! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["The queen forks the rook and the bishop: both can't be saved at once.","The next best move, 46…Qc4, would drop Black's winning chances from 48% to 11% (+5.67).","46…Qa5 threatens …Qxe1+, winning a rook, and stops Bd4.","It threatens …Qxe1+, winning a rook, so White has to spend the next move on it.","White was threatening Bd4, winning the queen and a rook, picking it up with 47.Qxe7. Qa5 takes care of it.","White answers 47.Bf2."]},{"ply":168,"name":"84…Be4","cls":"blunder","color":"b","headline":"84…Be4 is a blunder: Black's winning chances go from 42% to 21%.","points":["White answers 85.Kh3.","Better was 84…Kd5 (+0.93): the king steps out of the firing line (fewer enemy pieces aim at it now)."],"better":"84…Kd5 steps the king out of the firing line. Engine line: 85.f5 Ke4 86.Kh4 Kf3 87.f6 Bd5 (+0.93)."}],"opening":{"name":"King's Indian Defense: Fianchetto Variation, Kavalek Defense","eco":"E62","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 9.Re1: 17 moves in all, 9 by White and 8 by Black.","Theory runs out after 9.Re1: too few games between strong players reached this position to go further."]}}